props.description:
Cross-axis extent for an edge placement — the width of a side panel; a top or bottom
one sizes to its content and takes this as the ceiling. Named steps resolve to tokens;
any other CSS length is used as given. Ignored when centred.

Explanatory copy behind an info button on the title line — for a definition or caveat
too long for the description. A real focusable button, not a `title` attribute;
`strings.tooltip` names it.

Uploads: `onUpload`, `maxSize`, `maxFiles`, `accept`. Without `onUpload` there is no
attachment control. The uploader resolves to a `CommentAttachment` with a permanent `url`;
the composer submits what it returns, not the file it was given.

